---
description: Environment config via NestJS ConfigModule — no hardcoded secrets
globs: src/config/**,.env.example
alwaysApply: false
---

# Environment & Config

- Never hardcode values that vary by environment (URLs, secrets, feature flags)
- Feature code: `ConfigService` from `@nestjs/config` — **never** `process.env`
- Required vars: documented in `.env.example` with comments
- Config files: `src/config/` — one file per concern (`app`, `database`, `redis`, `jwt`)

When adding a new env var: update the matching config file **and** `.env.example`.
